'''Echo Echo''', formerly known as '''Echo''',{{Refn|Echo Echo was originally named Echo.{{Refn|[https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ben10/images/2/23/Hero_Generation_Series_Bible.pdf Hero Generation Series Bible]|group = HG Bible|name = bible}}{{Refn|[[:File:Echo Echo Concept Art by Glen Murakami.png]]|group = ca|name = glen}} The name briefly made it into the show as the alien addressed himself as such in ''[[Ben 10 Returns: Part 2]]''.|group = note}} is the [[Omnitrix]]'s DNA sample of a [[Sonorosian]]<ref>[[Thirteen]]</ref><ref name="I13>''[[Inspector 13]]''</ref> from the planet [[Sonorosia]].{{Refn|[[:File:Echo Echo Bandai Card.png]]|group = Bandai}}{{Refn|Echo Echo Plumber Database; [[:File:Echo Echo Plumber Database 1.png|file 1]]|group = AF VG|name = Echo Echo Plumber Database}}

==Appearance==
Echo Echo is a small, white humanoid made of silicon.<ref>[[Gwen Tennyson (Classic)|Gwen Tennyson]]</ref><ref>''[[Fool's Gold]]''</ref> His body is natural; although he strongly resembles a robot, he is neither it nor an animated containment suit.{{Refn|A fan once asked [[Dwayne McDuffie]] if Echo Echo was either a robot or some kind of living containment suit, and then shared a theory that Echo Echo's being is actually living sound waves for a containment suit to hold; Dwayne responded by saying "Echo [Echo] is a member of a race that just looks like that".{{Refn|[[:File:Omnitrix Transformation Duration.PNG]]|group = DM|name = archive}} Coincidentally, [[Derrick J. Wyatt]] later stated that Echo Echo was in fact a containment suit housing living sound waves while answering fan questions,{{Refn|[[:File:Conductoid Containment Suit.png]]|group = DJW|name = link2}}{{Refn|[[:File:Echo Echo Living Sound.png]]|group = DJW|name = link}} while specifying that he did not come up with the concept, only heard of it,{{Refn|[[:File:Echo Echo Living Sound 2.png]]|group = DJW}} and that it came from Dwayne McDuffie.{{Refn|[[:File:Echo Containment coming from Dwayne.png]]|group = DJW}} Due to the apparent contradiction, Echo Echo is not considered to have a containment suit.{{Refn|[[Ben 10 Planet:Longstanding Misinformation]]|group = BTP}}|group = note}} One of his most noticeable features is a square appendage resembling an MP3 player behind his back with a port on it, decorated with a 10 symbol and what looks like cassette tapes on his lower legs. The green circle-shaped indents on the back of Echo Echo's hands are sound holes which help him resonate,{{Refn|[[:File:Echo Echo Sound Holes.png]]|group = MW|name = hole}} and the inside of his mouth is also green with lines that give it the appearance of an amplifier. He also wears headphones so he would not be hurt by his own sonic screams.{{Refn|''link unavailable''|group = DM}} The headphones are attached to the appendage on his back.

In '''[[Ben 10: Alien Force (TV Series)|Alien Force]]''' and '''[[Ben 10: Ultimate Alien (TV Series)|Ultimate Alien]]''', Echo Echo wore the [[Omnitrix (Original)|original Omnitrix]]/[[Ultimatrix (Original)|Ultimatrix]] symbol on his chest.

In ''[[Ben 10-Generator Rex: Heroes United|Heroes United]]'', Echo Echo looked mostly the same as before, except his eyes were bigger and his mouth was recolored black.

In '''[[Ben 10: Omniverse (TV Series)|Omniverse]]''', Echo Echo's eyes bulge out, he has two black stripes on both of his earplugs, which are more pronounced, his legs are stubby, he now has three toes, and the green circles on his hands are now bigger. He is also shorter and has a circular shape on his stomach and the tapes on his legs are now gone. His head is less round and is wider and the outlines of his mouth and eyes are thicker as well as his wires. He wears the [[Omnitrix (Omniverse)|Omnitrix]] symbol on his forehead.

