====[[Ben 10: Alien Force (Video Game)|Ben 10: Alien Force]]====
Echo Echo is a playable alien character in the Nintendo DS version of the game.

Echo Echo is initially unavailable but is unlocked upon completion of the Shipyard 1-2 level.

Echo Echo is able to use sonic screams and up to six duplicates to chain various combo attacks.

Echo Echo is not required to be used at all in order to complete the game.

====[[Ben 10 Alien Force: Vilgax Attacks]]====
Echo Echo is a playable alien in the game.

=====Xbox 360, Nintendo Wii, PlayStation 2 and PlayStation Portable Versions=====
Due to the [[Omnitrix (Original)|Omnitrix]] rebooting after [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]]'s abuse of the quick-change feature during his battle with an animated [[Mr. Smoothy (Classic)|Mr. Smoothy]] mascot, Echo Echo was temporarily locked until Ben's arrival on [[Anur Phaetos]].

Echo Echo is able to duplicate himself up to two times, for a total of three Echo Echos at a time, in order to activate multiple pressure-sensitive platforms simultaneously.

Echo Echo is able to use his sonic screams to shatter obstructing crystals.

Wall of Sound is an unlockable combo move for Echo Echo.

Echo Echo is vital for progression on the Anur Phaetos and [[MorOtesi]] levels of the game.

=====Nintendo DS Version=====
Echo Echo and [[Chromastone (Classic)|Chromastone]] are reunlocked upon [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]]'s arrival on MorOtesi.

Echo Echo is able to use his sonic screams to shatter MorOtesi diamonds.

====[[Ben 10 Alien Force: The Rise of Hex]]====
Echo Echo is a playable alien in the game.

Due to the [[Omnitrix (Original)|Omnitrix]] shorting out after [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] fiddled with it, Echo Echo was temporarily locked until the beginning of Level 6.

Echo Echo is able to duplicate himself up to two times, for a total of three Echo Echoes at a time, in order to activate linked switches simultaneously for access to further areas. Each duplicate can be controlled separately.

Echo Echo's small size allows him to navigate areas that most of Ben's aliens and Ben himself are unable to access.

====[[Ben 10 Ultimate Alien: Cosmic Destruction]]====
Echo Echo is a playable alien in the game.

Similar to [[Spidermonkey (Classic)|Spidermonkey]], Echo Echo's small size allows him to fit into small passages other aliens cannot. Like in ''[[Ben 10 Alien Force: Vilgax Attacks|Vilgax Attacks]]'', Echo Echo can only clone himself to a maximum of three clones at a time. He can also go [[Ultimate Echo Echo#Video Games|Ultimate]].

Echo Echo is vital for progression on The Catacombs and The Amazon levels of the game. He is also the default optional alien for the Devil's Tower level.

